1
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:04,600
Job searching can feel like a second job,

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,100
switching sites, rereading requirements,

3
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:09,900
and wondering which application
deserves your time.

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:12,950
JobPilot helps you focus on roles worth pursuing.

5
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:19,050
For You replaces an endless feed
with three focused choices.

6
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:22,750
Each role shows why it was selected
using evidence fit, preferences,

7
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:25,450
location, and freshness.

8
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:27,550
The public demo uses synthetic data.

9
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:33,850
Open a role, and the decision comes first.

10
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:37,300
Fit Score, plain-language conclusion,
strong evidence, attention areas,

11
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:41,400
experience, practical fit,
and the employer destination.

12
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:45,350
Technical proof stays available when needed.

13
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:51,550
Application Strategy answers what
to emphasize, prepare, and clarify.

14
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:56,550
GPT-5.6 Sol created this prepared review
through Codex, not live inference,

15
00:00:56,550 --> 00:00:59,800
and it never calculates or changes

16
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,850
the deterministic Fit Score.

17
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:08,700
The Evidence view separates strong support,

18
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:12,300
partial support, missing evidence,
and items needing review.

19
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:15,350
Capability names stay readable,

20
00:01:15,350 --> 00:01:17,850
while exact proof remains available
on demand.

21
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,300
Score Proof shows the 100-point contract.

22
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:26,700
Deterministic AI Fit V2.2 calculates every score,

23
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:29,700
while the Technical Ledger preserves exact arithmetic

24
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:31,350
with zero hidden adjustments.

25
00:01:33,830 --> 00:01:36,500
Every Score Receipt is independently verifiable.

26
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:39,200
A valid receipt fully reproduces the score,

27
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,850
while a tampered receipt becomes invalid.

28
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:47,600
JobPilot opens the employer
destination deliberately.

29
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:52,400
It never fills forms, sends resumes,
redirects, or submits applications.

30
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:55,950
This public demo uses a fictional employer page.

31
00:01:58,420 --> 00:02:02,500
Saving a role updates only browser-local planning.

32
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:06,700
The tracker supports Saved, Interested,
Preparing, and Applied.

33
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:09,950
Applied is only a planning label.

34
00:02:09,950 --> 00:02:13,450
JobPilot never auto-applies.

35
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:20,250
Gemma 4 12B is the primary local semantic model.

36
00:02:20,250 --> 00:02:24,700
Deterministic code calculates every Fit Score.

37
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:30,300
GPT-5.6 Sol adds prepared strategy and critique
through Codex, not live inference.

38
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:35,250
Codex also helped build, debug, repair,
and test the product.

39
00:02:35,250 --> 00:02:39,150
OpenAI API requests and cost are zero.

40
00:02:41,650 --> 00:02:44,250
Fit Score is not a hiring probability.

41
00:02:44,250 --> 00:02:47,400
JobPilot helps people spend less time
decoding job posts

42
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:50,050
and more time acting on roles that fit.

